{"track":"precalc","num":"3.03","slug":"sum-and-difference-formulas","title":"Sum and Difference Formulas","sections":[{"heading":"Section 1: Sine Sum and Difference Identities","questions":[{"q":"State the formula for $\\sin(A + B)$.","choices":["$\\sin A\\cos B + \\cos A\\sin B$","$\\sin A\\cos B - \\cos A\\sin B$","$\\cos A\\cos B - \\sin A\\sin B$","$\\sin A + \\sin B$"],"correct":0,"answer":"The sine sum formula is $\\sin(A + B) = \\sin A\\cos B + \\cos A\\sin B$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2*cos(x) + 1"],"xmin":-3.14,"xmax":6.28,"ymin":-1.5,"ymax":3.5,"points":[[0,3],[3.14,-1]],"width":145}},{"q":"Find the exact value of $\\sin(75^\\circ)$ using $75^\\circ = 45^\\circ + 30^\\circ$.","choices":["$\\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}$","$\\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4}$","$\\frac{\\sqrt{3} + 1}{2}$","$\\frac{\\sqrt{2} + 1}{2}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\sin(45^\\circ)\\cos(30^\\circ) + \\cos(45^\\circ)\\sin(30^\\circ) = \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}$."},{"q":"Simplify $\\sin(x + \\pi)$.","choices":["$-\\sin x$","$\\sin x$","$-\\cos x$","$\\cos x$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\sin x\\cos\\pi + \\cos x\\sin\\pi = \\sin x(-1) + \\cos x(0) = -\\sin x$."}]},{"heading":"Section 2: Cosine Sum and Difference Identities","questions":[{"q":"State the formula for $\\cos(A - B)$.","choices":["$\\cos A\\cos B + \\sin A\\sin B$","$\\cos A\\cos B - \\sin A\\sin B$","$\\sin A\\sin B - \\cos A\\cos B$","$\\cos A - \\cos B$"],"correct":0,"answer":"The cosine difference formula is $\\cos(A - B) = \\cos A\\cos B + \\sin A\\sin B$."},{"q":"Find the exact value of $\\cos(15^\\circ)$ using $15^\\circ = 45^\\circ - 30^\\circ$.","choices":["$\\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}$","$\\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4}$","$\\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{4}$","$\\frac{\\sqrt{2} + 1}{4}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\cos(45^\\circ)\\cos(30^\\circ) + \\sin(45^\\circ)\\sin(30^\\circ) = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["sin(x) + cos(x)"],"xmin":-3.14,"xmax":6.28,"ymin":-2,"ymax":2,"points":[[0.785,1.414]],"width":145}},{"q":"Simplify $\\cos(x - \\pi/2)$.","choices":["$\\sin x$","$-\\sin x$","$\\cos x$","$-\\cos x$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\cos x\\cos(\\pi/2) + \\sin x\\sin(\\pi/2) = \\cos x(0) + \\sin x(1) = \\sin x$."}]},{"heading":"Section 3: Tangent Sum and Difference Identities","questions":[{"q":"State the formula for $\\tan(A + B)$.","choices":["$\\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A\\tan B}$","$\\frac{\\tan A - \\tan B}{1 + \\tan A\\tan B}$","$\\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 + \\tan A\\tan B}$","$\\tan A + \\tan B$"],"correct":0,"answer":"The tangent sum formula is $\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A\\tan B}$."},{"q":"If $\\tan A = 1/2$ and $\\tan B = 1/3$, find $\\tan(A + B)$.","choices":["$1$","$5/6$","$5/7$","$2/3$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\frac{1/2 + 1/3}{1 - (1/2)(1/3)} = \\frac{5/6}{1 - 1/6} = \\frac{5/6}{5/6} = 1$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\frac{\\tan(80^\\circ) - \\tan(20^\\circ)}{1 + \\tan(80^\\circ)\\tan(20^\\circ)}$.","choices":["$\\sqrt{3}$","$1/\\sqrt{3}$","$1$","$0$"],"correct":0,"answer":"This matches the formula for $\\tan(80^\\circ - 20^\\circ) = \\tan(60^\\circ) = \\sqrt{3}$.","figure":{"type":"triangle","vertices":[[0,0],[5.5,0],[2.1,3.8]],"labels":["A","B","C"],"angle_marks":[{"vertex":0,"label":"52°"},{"vertex":1,"label":"63°"}],"fill":true,"width":145}}]},{"heading":"Section 4: Compound Angle Problems with Given Ratios","questions":[{"q":"Given $\\sin\\alpha = 3/5$ (Quadrant I) and $\\cos\\beta = -5/13$ (Quadrant II), find $\\sin(\\alpha + \\beta)$.","choices":["$33/65$","$-33/65$","$63/65$","$-63/65$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\cos\\alpha = 4/5$. $\\sin\\beta = \\sqrt{1 - (-5/13)^2} = 12/13$. $\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta) = \\sin\\alpha\\cos\\beta + \\cos\\alpha\\sin\\beta = (3/5)(-5/13) + (4/5)(12/13) = -15/65 + 48/65 = 33/65$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["3*cos(0.5*x)"],"xmin":-3.14,"xmax":6.28,"ymin":-3.5,"ymax":3.5,"points":[[0,3],[3.14,0]],"width":145}},{"q":"For the same angles ($\\cos\\alpha = 4/5, \\sin\\alpha = 3/5, \\cos\\beta = -5/13, \\sin\\beta = 12/13$), find $\\cos(\\alpha + \\beta)$.","choices":["$-56/65$","$56/65$","$-16/65$","$16/65$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta) = \\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta - \\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta = (4/5)(-5/13) - (3/5)(12/13) = -20/65 - 36/65 = -56/65$."},{"q":"In which quadrant does $\\alpha + \\beta$ lie in the previous problems?","choices":["Quadrant II","Quadrant I","Quadrant III","Quadrant IV"],"correct":0,"answer":"Since $\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta) = -56/65 < 0$ and $\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta) = 33/65 > 0$, the angle $\\alpha + \\beta$ terminates in Quadrant II."}]}]}